                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Part 2 in the Enigmatis series.\n\nThis is a direct continuation of the first game, though you don't really need to have played the first part.\n\nThe hidden object formula has changed a bit. Instead of simply finding objects in the scenes, you now need to solve some additional simple puzzles to obtain all items. I really liked this approach.\n\nThe scenes are beautifully drawn. But, as usual in this genre, the animations and voice-overs are low-budget and sometimes even silly.\n\nI had no issues getting through most of the game. Only towards the end did things get a bit confusing, probably because I was getting tired. I played the game for several hours straight and finished it in two long sessions.\n\nA casual, light horror puzzle game, perfect for the Halloween season.",
